</ul></nav></section><section class="front-matter"><div class="ameta p font-secondary font-xs">
<hgroup><h1>Conservative and liberal attitudes drive polarized neural responses to political content</h1></hgroup><div class="cg p">
<a href='https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term="Leong%20YC"[Author]' class="usa-link" aria-describedby="id1"><span class="name western">Yuan Chang Leong</span></a><div hidden="hidden" id="id1">
<h3><span class="name western">Yuan Chang Leong</span></h3>
<div class="p">
<sup>a</sup>Helen Wills Neuroscience Institute, University of California, Berkeley, CA 94720;</div>
<div class="p">Find articles by <a href='https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term="Leong%20YC"[Author]' class="usa-link"><span class="name western">Yuan Chang Leong</span></a>
</div>
</div>
<sup>a,</sup><sup>1</sup>, <a href='https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term="Chen%20J"[Author]' class="usa-link" aria-describedby="id2"><span class="name western">Janice Chen</span></a><div hidden="hidden" id="id2">
<h3><span class="name western">Janice Chen</span></h3>
<div class="p">
<sup>b</sup>Department of Psychological and Brain Sciences, Johns Hopkins University, Baltimore, MD 21218;</div>
<div class="p">Find articles by <a href='https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term="Chen%20J"[Author]' class="usa-link"><span class="name western">Janice Chen</span></a>
</div>
</div>
<sup>b</sup>, <a href='https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term="Willer%20R"[Author]' class="usa-link" aria-describedby="id3"><span class="name western">Robb Willer</span></a><div hidden="hidden" id="id3">
